dsh: reasoning:
So plan's claim "All 6 templates silently cut skills to 5 per group (render-caps.ts)" appears in v1 findings and v2 section 2. It says "All 6 templates silently cut skills to 5 per group" — correct. But it also says "the `.slice()` caps and `render-caps.ts` go away". render-caps.ts is a *detection* module used by chat tools, not a cause of truncation. Removing it is only possible after removing the slice() caps. But the plan phrasing lumps them. Actually "the `.slice()` caps and `render-caps.ts` go away" means after removing caps, render-caps is dead. Fine, minor.

But more importantly: removing caps has layout implications - plan says "layouts wrap to fit every skill". German-ats sidebar is 52mm and fixed 52mm width; unbounded skill lists will overflow the page and can't page-break because the two-column flex container... Actually plan says sidebar background repeats on every page, but a CSS flexbox two-column layout does not fragment into columns across pages in Chromium print. It paginates by slicing the whole block vertically, leaving the sidebar content only on page 1 while the main column continues. Wait — with flex, fragmentation is not supported well: Chromium will break inside a flex item, but the sibling sidebar won't repeat. So a 2-page German CV with a left sidebar will show sidebar content only on page 1 (or overflow/clip), because the sidebar and main are in one flex container and Chromium fragments the flex container: each page gets a slice of the flex container. In a row-direction flex, content is laid out horizontally and pages break vertically; each page shows the same two columns for that vertical slice but the next page slice shows blank sidebar area. So sidebar doesn't repeat. Plan claims "The sidebar background repeats on every page" - that's only true if it uses a page-background technique that repeats, e.g. `@page` background or a fixed-position background per page. CSS `position: fixed` in print repeats on each page in Chromium. But the sidebar *content* wouldn't repeat. Plan says "sidebar background repeats on every page", not content. But the real issue is sidebar content (skills, certs) will be only on page 1 and if it's longer than a page it will overflow into... hmm. Actually in flex fragmentation, the aside content itself fragments; but because the main column is taller, the flex container's height is main's height, and aside only occupies top. Page 2 has empty sidebar. That's actually acceptable visually if background repeats, though it wastes space and the last page has a big empty left column. But if the sidebar is longer than page 1, does it overflow? The flex container's cross-size is max of items; aside could be taller than main, making container taller. Then page 1 shows first slice; page 2 shows rest of aside and remaining main. It may work but with overflow issues. Not a critical finding but a fidelity risk worth noting. The plan's spike 0b should test 2-page two-column. It says spike 0b "on one template with fonts, photo and tagging" — not a 2-page German CV. The eval does include a 2-page German fixture; that's later (PR 3), but fine.

Now let me check the catalog and templates for actual page size / margins. Plan says US templates Letter 0.5-0.75in margins. Let's check one template: USPremiumATSTemplate.
