Now, a big factual issue: Plan says "All 6 templates use Arial body + Georgia headers (system fonts, ATS-compliant)" per AGENTS. Plan proposes self-hosted Arimo/Gelasio "metric-compatible". For ATS, fine. But "Arimo and Gelasio ... bound explicitly in the templates" — Gelasio metric-compatible with Georgia. Is Gelasio actually metric-compatible with Georgia? Gelasio is metric-compatible with Georgia (per Google Fonts, yes). Arimo is metrically compatible with Arial. Good.

But in Browser Run Chromium with self-hosted base64 fonts: Cloudflare Browser Rendering `/pdf` explicitly does NOT support web fonts? Let me check. I recall docs: "The PDF endpoint supports only system fonts. Custom fonts are not supported" — maybe that was for `/pdf` in a 2024 version. Let me web search to verify current state (2026-ish docs in this fictional timeline, but we have web access; treat results as data).

